 ## Overview
-TideGS Trajectory Ordering is a training strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting that replaces standard randomized view shuffling with a trajectory-aware ordered sequence of views to improve optimization stability and convergence for large-scale scenes [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard 3DGS by preserving trajectory continuity, which reduces gradient variation between consecutive optimization steps, while relying on visibility-induced sparsity to mitigate the risks of sequential correlation [S1, unofficial].
+TideGS Trajectory Ordering is a training strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting that replaces standard randomized view shuffling with a trajectory-aware ordered sequence of views to improve optimization stability and convergence for large-scale scenes [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard 3DGS which samples views with random shuffling, TideGS uses a clustered traveling-salesperson (TSP) ordering to preserve trajectory continuity, reducing gradient variation between consecutive steps [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Base 3DGS Optimization](7549-base-3d-gaussian-splatting-optimization.md) by modifying the view sampling schedule while retaining the standard masked update mechanism.
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs**
-*   **Inputs:** A set of $M$ training views with camera poses; a set of 3D Gaussian primitives with parameters $\theta$; a fixed block size $B$.
-*   **Outputs:** A permutation $\pi$ of view indices; an ordered training loop that processes views according to $\pi$.
